{"name":"Amorphous Rose","hex":"#b1a7b7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amorphous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lacking a definite form or clear shape.","Being without definite character or nature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amorphous"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amorphous solid","blocks":[{"text":"In condensed matter physics and materials science, an amorphous solid, or non-crystalline solid, is a solid that lacks the long-range order that is a characteristic of a crystal. The terms \"glass\" and \"glassy solid\" are sometimes used synonymously with amorphous solid; however, these terms refer specifically to amorphous materials that undergo a glass transition. Examples of amorphous solids include glasses, metallic glasses, and certain types of plastics and polymers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amorphous_solid","wikidata":"Q103382"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Crystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png/500px-Crystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Crystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png/1280px-Crystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Crystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png/500px-Crystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crystalline vs. amorphous solid","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrystalline_vs._Amorphous_solid.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Lake_Mj%C3%B8sa_sunrise_reflected_in_window_01.jpg/500px-Lake_Mj%C3%B8sa_sunrise_reflected_in_window_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Lake_Mj%C3%B8sa_sunrise_reflected_in_window_01.jpg/1280px-Lake_Mj%C3%B8sa_sunrise_reflected_in_window_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Lake_Mj%C3%B8sa_sunrise_reflected_in_window_01.jpg/500px-Lake_Mj%C3%B8sa_sunrise_reflected_in_window_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glass is a c